From 93df7ea60bf742ff8a5ef9b4ee1d11f1d3f7ebc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Phan <seanphan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 08:20:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] path3: port bias_vl image-routing hunks onto SM80 fork
 (step 2/5)

Hand-ports the vision-only hunks from the pinned Vision-Exp head's MoE
routing chain onto the proven SM80 fork, keeping the fork's existing
ampere_sparse SM80 attention backend untouched.

- csrc/libtorch_stable/moe/{moe_ops.h,torch_bindings.cpp,
  topk_softplus_sqrt_kernels.cu}: add bias_vl/image_sentinel_lo to the
  topk_softplus_sqrt native op (declaration, schema, and both the fast
  hash-table kernel and the generic templated kernel), so image
  sentinel tokens route by bias_vl instead of the text correction
  bias or hash table, even inside hash-MoE-compiled kernel instances.
- vllm/_custom_ops.py: thread the two new params through the Python
  op wrapper.
- vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/dsv4_topk.py: extend
  the Triton fast-path kernel with an optional per-row image-bias
  override.
- vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_bias_router.py:
  thread bias_vl/image_sentinel_lo through the native-op call sites,
  the dsv4_topk fast-path gate (now excluded when a hash table is
  present), and the pure-PyTorch fallback scoring path.
- vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/router_factory.py,
  vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/layer.py: plumb the new
  parameters through the router factory and FusedMoEFactory.
- vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py: create gate.bias_vl and
  image_sentinel_lo on vision checkpoints (including on hash-MoE
  layers), pass them into FusedMoEFactory, and require input_ids
  when bias_vl routing is active.
- vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py: keep input_ids on non-first PP
  ranks so downstream vision-aware MoE layers can see them.

Deliberately NOT ported: the pinned head's unrelated removal of the
SM90-only dsv3_router_gemm kernel (non-vision divergence); MegaMoE
shared-expert/sequence-parallel refactors (SM90+-only, do not execute
on SM80); XPU-only fallback code paths (no XPU support in this fork).
